new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0b5a97f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/orchestrator/nanojev_real/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@
+# R02 frozen fixtures and the SDK acceptance runner
+
+Frozen, implementation-independent evaluation material for the NanoJev decision
+integration (plan `HTN-Jev专项测试需求-2026-09-19.md`, section 5 R02 and section 6).
+
+Everything in this directory is **data**. It does not import the model layer, and
+the expected answers were written *before* any model was run. These fixtures feed
+`scripts/nanojev_sdk_acceptance.py`, which crosses the real SDK stack
+(runtime → `NanoJevDecisionProvider` → `DecisionService`) and writes raw output to
+`.local-test-evidence/`, never to git.
+
+## The 12 fixtures
+
+| Group | Count | Files | Decision types |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `clear_preferred` | 4 | `r02_clear_priority_01/02`, `r02_clear_retry_01/02` | both |
+| `paired_context_change` | 4 | `r02_context_priority_01/02`, `r02_context_retry_01/02` | both |
+| `ambiguous_legal_set` | 4 | `r02_ambiguous_priority_01/02`, `r02_ambiguous_retry_01/02` | both |
+
+Both legal types (`ready_task_priority`, `retry_or_escalate`) appear in all three
+groups. Candidate ids are stable strings (`candidate-a`, `retry-same-task`, …);
+comparison is always by id, never by list position.
+
+**Clear (4).** Several legal candidates, the goal clearly favours one. One case
+per pair deliberately disagrees with the frozen Existing selector
+(`agreement_with_existing: false`), so agreement and correctness can never be
+read as the same number.
+
+**Paired context change (4).** Each is a copy of a clear case with exactly one
+decisive fact flipped, recorded in `changed_fact`. The two priority pairs and the
+two retry pairs invert each other, so a model that always picks the first
+candidate fails both directions of at least one pair.
+
+**Ambiguous (4).** `expected_selected` is `null` and `accepted_set` holds two or
+more legal answers. These test that the distribution *need not* concentrate —
+no single forced answer is invented for them.
+
+### Fixture fields
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `fixture_id` | Stable id, also used as the `decision_id` in the request |
+| `group` | `clear_preferred` / `paired_context_change` / `ambiguous_legal_set` |
+| `pairs_with` | For paired cases, the clear fixture it modifies |
+| `changed_fact` | The one decisive fact that changed, in plain words |
+| `decision_type` | One of the two legal R02 types |
+| `candidates` | `{id, label, metadata}`; at least two, labels short enough for a 512-token budget |
+| `context` | Concise goal summary, blocking gap and notes |
+| `expected_selected` | The intended answer, or `null` when ambiguous |
+| `accepted_set` | Every answer that is acceptable; the legal set for ambiguous cases |
+| `existing_selector` | What the frozen Existing path picks (production baseline) |
+| `agreement_with_existing` | Whether the intended answer matches that baseline |
+| `reason` | One-line justification, since quality is graded against it |
+
+## Running the runner
+
+Freeze check only — no model, no API, safe anywhere:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/nanojev_sdk_acceptance.py
+```
+
+It prints every fixture SHA256 plus a combined digest, validates the 4/4/4
+composition, and writes `r02_fixture_freeze.json`.
+
+Live run — once `LocalNanoJevRuntime` exists and its constructor is readable:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/nanojev_sdk_acceptance.py \
+    --runtime-module agent_orchestrator.decision.local_runtime \
+    --runtime-class LocalNanoJevRuntime \
+    --runtime-kwargs '{"model_path": "<checkpoint>"}' \
+    --mode shadow
+```
+
+The runner deliberately does **not** construct the local runtime itself. That
+class belongs to `decision/local_runtime.py`, owned by another agent; until it
+is readable, the script refuses to guess its signature and prints the required
+invocation instead of silently passing.
+
+The runtime must implement the SDK ABC in
+`src/agent_orchestrator/decision/runtime.py`
+(`start` / `evaluate(NanoJevRequest) -> NanoJevOutput` / `close`). The runner
+wraps it in the real provider and the real `DecisionService`; a cache predictor
+is never called directly, because acceptance has to cross
+runtime → provider → service.
+
+## What the run produces
+
+* **R01-style smoke**: at least two legal candidates per request through
+  `NanoJevDecisionProvider`, plus a real `DecisionService` shadow pass that
+  preserves the frozen Existing answer.
+* **R02**: the 12 fixtures once each, then the 6 clear cases with the candidate
+  order reversed. Answers are compared by stable id.
+* **Validity**: finite probabilities in `[0, 1]`, full candidate-id coverage,
+  sum to 1 within `1e-5`. Adapter errors are retained, never swallowed.
+* **Accuracy vs agreement, separately**: per-type hits against `expected_selected`
+  and per-case agreement against `existing_selector` are distinct fields.
+  `definite_hits` is not production readiness, and
+  `agreement_with_existing` is not correctness.
+* **Measurement**: model load time recorded apart from warm latency, 5 warmups
+  then 20 samples, warm p50/p95 and an error count. Few samples — p99 is not
+  reported and none of this is a product SLA.
+* **Evidence**: all raw output lands in
+  `.local-test-evidence/<date>/sdk-nanojev-integration/real/`, which is
+  gitignored.
+
+## Boundaries
+
+* No model is loaded at import time, and no unexpected API call happens.
+* These 12+6 samples **cannot** justify promoting NanoJev to Primary; the runner
+  says so in its own output and this directory makes no such claim.
+* An unavailable model, device or service is recorded as `BLOCKED_ENV` — never
+  as a pass — and the fixtures do not change when a run fails.
+
+Frozen set digest: `f77397a8c3ba647bbfafefde1dc939c7bc7d3ec4faa291ca9d981cf30613a3bd`
+(recomputed and printed by every run; per-file hashes are in the freeze record).
